* [HIP] feat(moe): fused route-sort + MXFP4 activation-quant kernel for gfx950 decode

Add mxfp4_moe_sort_quant_fwd: a single-launch HIP kernel that fuses opus
route sorting, BF16->MXFP4 activation quantization (v_cvt_scalef32_pk_fp4_bf16)
and routed-output zeroing for the Qwen3.5 MXFP4 MoE decode path (model_dim=4096,
block_m=32, M in [1,128], routes (num_experts,topk) in {(512,10),(513,11)}).

CTA 0 builds the sorted metadata via an LDS expert histogram + DPP wave
prefix-scan; the remaining CTAs emit compact per-token E8M0 scales that the
flydsl GEMM1 consumes directly. Gated behind SGLANG_AITER_FUSED_DECODE_SORT_QUANT
and fed into fused_moe_2stages as prequantized_a1 on the expanded-scale path.

Adds an op_test (correctness vs opus + generic quant, decode-M gate, runtime-arch
gate, CUDA-graph replay) and a sort+quant latency benchmark.

