* [HIP] [OPUS] refactor(moe): auto-gate fused decode sort+quant, drop env var

Address review feedback on PR #6165:

- Remove the SGLANG_AITER_FUSED_DECODE_SORT_QUANT env gate (and the dead
  compact-scale env). The fused route-sort + MXFP4 quant kernel is now
  selected purely from the gfx950/shape/dtype/route gate and falls back to
  the generic sort+quant otherwise -- an AITER core optimization should not
  depend on a downstream-specific runtime switch. Add an internal
  _fused_decode_sort_quant_disabled hook for same-build base-vs-head A/B.

- Fold the standalone op_tests/test_mxfp4_fused_sort_quant.py cases into the
  existing op_tests/test_moe_sorting_mxfp4.py operator-family harness (gate
  table, runtime-arch dispatch, disable toggle, wrapper, CUDA-graph replay,
  and per-route correctness+latency); remove the standalone file. The hip
  benchmark under op_benchmarks/hip/ stays separate.

